1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,233
In Orlando, Florida, there is an organization that believes every girl deserves to grow into a confident, capable woman.

2
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:26,833
Empowered Girls, founded in twenty eighteen, works with girls across Orange County through life skills, mentorship, health and wellness, and academics infused with empowerment.

3
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:39,700
Their mission, in their own words: empowering girls to grow into confident, capable women through life skills, mentorship, and programs that help them overcome barriers and achieve success.

4
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:43,767
The work happens in a county of real scale.

5
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:48,167
Orange County is home to more than three hundred twenty-two thousand children —

6
00:00:48,167 --> 00:00:49,733
about one in five residents.

7
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:53,533
And about one in six of those children lives below the poverty line.

8
00:00:55,533 --> 00:00:58,667
Nationally, the picture for girls is just as urgent.

9
00:00:58,667 --> 00:01:03,733
By fifth grade, only sixty-eight percent of girls describe themselves as confident —

10
00:01:03,733 --> 00:01:06,567
down from eighty-six percent six years earlier.

11
00:01:06,567 --> 00:01:12,633
And by one national estimate, one in three young people reach adulthood without ever having a mentor.

12
00:01:12,633 --> 00:01:15,267
This is the field Empowered Girls stands in.

13
00:01:17,767 --> 00:01:22,767
But no mission exists in isolation. Around this work is a larger ecosystem —

14
00:01:22,767 --> 00:01:28,533
funders, schools, government programs, community organizations, businesses, and people —

15
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:32,800
who may already be aligned with what Empowered Girls is building.

16
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,433
Anansi Atlas exists to map exactly that.

17
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:38,333
Start with funding.

18
00:01:38,333 --> 00:01:44,200
In Central Florida, the pathways potentially aligned with girls' youth development are real and specific.

19
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:48,900
A community foundation whose grassroots grants name youth development as a priority.

20
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:53,033
A local charity with a microgrant program built for smaller organizations.

21
00:01:53,033 --> 00:02:00,200
And corporate giving from the region's largest employers, with youth and education programs that accept applications year-round.

22
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:05,267
None of these are commitments. Every one is a doorway —

23
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:08,800
worth researching, worth confirming, worth a conversation.

24
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:16,967
Then, partners. Orange County Public Schools runs a formal Partners in Education program —

25
00:02:16,967 --> 00:02:20,600
the front door for organizations that work inside schools.

26
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:27,267
The University of Central Florida connects student volunteers to more than two hundred community agencies.

27
00:02:27,267 --> 00:02:33,600
And Rollins College runs an institute whose entire purpose is strengthening Orange County nonprofits.

28
00:02:35,267 --> 00:02:37,400
Government has doorways of its own.

29
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:43,833
Orange County's Citizens' Commission for Children reviews funding for youth-serving nonprofits every year.

30
00:02:43,833 --> 00:02:48,933
Community Development Block Grants support programs for families who need them most.

31
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:53,967
And the City of Orlando builds neighborhood initiatives through nonprofit partners.

32
00:02:53,967 --> 00:02:57,667
Possible pathways — each with its own eligibility to confirm.

33
00:02:59,533 --> 00:03:02,833
And alongside opportunity, an honest look inward.

34
00:03:02,833 --> 00:03:06,400
The platform reads readiness the way a funder would —

35
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:10,700
program documentation, outcome tracking, partnership materials —

36
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:16,767
and shows where an organization is strong, and where to strengthen next. Not as criticism.

37
00:03:16,767 --> 00:03:17,767
As preparation.

38
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:26,367
All of it comes together here. This is Empowered Girls' actual workspace in Anansi Atlas —

39
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:32,567
live in production today. Their mission at the center. Around it, the funders. The partners.

40
00:03:32,567 --> 00:03:36,200
The government pathways. The resources. The readiness.

41
00:03:37,733 --> 00:03:43,300
From here, research becomes decisions. What to pursue. Who to call. What to prepare.

42
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:44,833
In order, starting now.

43
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:50,200
It ends in a plan — a thirty-day sequence of clear next actions.

44
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:53,500
Confirm eligibility for the strongest funding pathways.

45
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,967
Open the school partnership conversation.

46
00:03:55,967 --> 00:04:01,567
Assemble the readiness documents that outreach will ask for. Small steps, in the right order.

47
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:06,600
This is the web surrounding Empowered Girls —

48
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:13,133
built around their mission, their location, the girls they serve, their priorities, and their capacity today.

49
00:04:13,133 --> 00:04:16,733
Every organization's web looks different. That is the point.

50
00:04:16,733 --> 00:04:22,633
Anansi Atlas helps nonprofit leaders see what surrounds their mission, and decide what to do next.

51
00:04:24,967 --> 00:04:30,633
Your mission is already surrounded by people, resources, pathways, and possibilities.

52
00:04:30,633 --> 00:04:35,700
The next step is seeing how they connect. Call us, or visit anansiatlas.com.

53
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:37,833
Your organization could be next.
